hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3631","Harun bin Abdullah Al-Hammal told me, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Habib Basri, told us, on the authority of Amr bin Haram Basri, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, and Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “Dabaa wanted to perform Hajj, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded her to do so.” She made a condition, so she did it on the command of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3632","Imran ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed me, he said: Shuaib informed me, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard a peacock, And Ikrimah, narrating on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “Duba’ah bint al-Zubayr came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Oh Messenger of God, I am a heavy woman, and I want to perform Hajj. How do you order me to perform the rituals of prayer? He said: “My family and stipulate that my place is where you have detained me.”"
"3633","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh reported, he said: Abd al-Razzaq reported, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Dabaa’ah, and she said: O Messenger of By God, I am complaining, and I want to perform Hajj, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Perform Hajj and stipulate that my place is where you detained me.” I said. By Abd al-Razzaq, both of them, on the authority of Aisha, Hisham, and al-Zuhri, who said: Yes. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know of anyone who narrated this. Hadith on the authority of Al-Zuhri, other than Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar"
"3634","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, he said: Abu Al-Numan told us, meaning Arim Muhammad bin Al-Fadl, he said: Thabit bin Yazid told us Abu Zaid Al-Ahwal said: Hilal bin Khabbab told us, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about a man who performs Hajj with stipulations? He said: “The condition between people,” so I told him, meaning Ikrimah, and he told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that Daba’ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib She came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I want to perform Hajj, so how should I say it? And my abode from the earth where you confine me, for indeed you have from your Lord what you have set aside.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3635","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh al-Misri and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Wahb, who said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, who said: “Ibn Umar used to deny the requirement for Hajj, and he would say: Is not the Sunnah of the Messenger of God sufficient for you? May God’s prayers and peace be upon him? If one of you is prevented from performing Hajj, he should circumambulate the House, Safa, and Marwah, then free himself from everything until he performs Hajj the next year. And he guides himself and fasts if he does not find any guidance.”"
"3636","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, “that he used to deny Stipulating Hajj, and saying: The Sunnah of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is not sufficient for you. He did not stipulate, so if one of you is imprisoned, So let him come to the House and circumambulate it and between Safa and Marwah, then let him shave and cut his hair, then let him perform Hajj, and he must perform Hajj from the beginning.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3637","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani reported, saying: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Thawr al-San’ani, narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and informed Ya’qub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi. He said: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, And Marwan bin Al-Hakam said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out at the time of Hudaybiyyah with some ten hundred of his companions, even though they were “By Dhu al-Hulayfah, he tied the sacrificial animal and wore his hair and entered ihram for the Umrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3638","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Waki’ told us, saying: Falah bin Humaid told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “Peace and blessings of God be upon him.”"
"3639","Mujahid bin Musa Baghdadi reported, on the authority of Hushaym, meaning Ibn Bashir, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt a camel on the right side, and blood dripped from it and he imitated it.”"
"3640","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs Al-Falas, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Sa’id Al-Qattan, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan Al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Dhul-Hulayfah, he passed by his body and felt it in its hump from the right side.” Then blood dripped from it, and he put two sandals on it, then he rode his camel, and when it came to rest with him on al-Bayda, he was welcomed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3641","Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, and Amra bint Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, that She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give gifts from Medina, so he twisted the necklaces of his gift, and then he would not avoid anything that he avoided.” “Muharram”"
"3642","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani reported, saying: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Harun, saying: Yahya bin Sa’id, meaning Al-Ansari, reported on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I used to twist the necklaces of the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would send them with them, and then “Whatever is lawful will come before the sacrificial animal reaches Mecca.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3643","Abu Hafs reported to Amr bin Ali, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Al-Qattan, he said: Ismail told us, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Amer told us, meaning Ibn Sharaheel Al-Shaabi, on the authority of Masruq, meaning Ibn Al-Ajda’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “If I were to twist the necklaces of the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he greeted, then he remains in ihram and does not enter ihram.”"
"3644","Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Da’eef told me, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, meaning the blind man, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I used to twist necklaces to follow the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would imitate his guidance, then he would send it back, then he would establish He should not avoid anything that a person in ihram avoids.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3645","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani reported, on the authority of Ubaida, meaning Ibn Humaid, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “You saw me twisting the necklaces of sheep to guide the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then he remained lawful.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3646","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani reported, saying: Hussein, meaning Ibn Hassan, told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of the Mother of the Believers, she said: “I So I took those necklaces from a curse that we had, and then what became lawful among us comes from its family, and what a man does from his family.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3647","Muhammad ibn Salamah reported to Abu al-Harith al-Masry, saying: Ibn al-Qasim reported, saying: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, On the authority of Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: “O Messenger of God, what is the matter with the people? They have become permissible for Umrah and you are not permissible.” Who is your Umrah? He said: I have tied my head and tied my Hadi, so I will not be permissible until I sacrifice. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3648","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed Abu Qudamah Al-Sarkhasi narrated, saying: Muadh, meaning Ibn Hisham Al-Dastawai, narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Abu Hassan al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Dhul-Hulayfah, he saw the sacrificial animal from the side of the hump.” Then he wiped the blood from it, put two sandals on it, then mounted his camel, and when it came to rest with him at Al-Bayda, he responded and entered into ihram at noon. And the Hajj was declared worthy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3649","Ahmad bin Harb Al-Mawsili reported, saying: Al-Qasim, who is Ibn Yazid, narrated to us, saying: Aflah, meaning Ibn Humaid, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad. On the authority of Aisha, she said: “I twisted the chains on the body of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with my hand, then he tied them, braided them, and directed them to the house, and he sent it there and resided, and whatever was forbidden to him was lawful for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3650","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I twisted necklaces The body of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he did not enter ihram and did not leave any clothing behind.”"
"3651","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari reported, saying: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I used to twist the necklaces of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, into sheep.”"
"3652","Ismail bin Masoud reported, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to guide sheep and imitate them.”"
"3653","Hanad bin Al-Sari Al-Kufi reported, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, meaning Muhammad bin Hazim, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, once gave a sheep as a gift and he imitated it.” On the authority of Ibn Bashar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Shu’bah, both of them are Sufyan, and Shu’bah on the authority of Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Abraham with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3654","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, told us, saying: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, told us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I used to twist the necklaces of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, into sheep and then he would not enter into ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3655","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “I used to twist the necklaces of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for sheep, and then he would not enter ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3656","Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Bistami Al-Qumsi reported, saying: Abd Al-Samad told us, meaning Ibn Abd Al-Warith, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jehad, and I am Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith. He said: Abu Muammar, meaning the companion of Abd al-Warith, told me: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Muhammad bin Juhadah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “We used to imitate The sheep will be sent with it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as permissible and not deprived of anything.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3657","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told me, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Hisham Al-Dastawi told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of my father Hassan Al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Dhul-Hulayfah, he felt the sacrificial animal from the side of the right hump. Then he wiped the blood from him, then he put two sandals on him, then he mounted his camel, and when it mounted him at Al-Bayda, he entered ihram, and he entered ihram at noon and his family. \By Hajj\"""""
"3658","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “They were present with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. In Medina, he will send a sacrificial animal, and whoever wishes may enter into ihram, and whoever will may leave it.”"
"3659","Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Kawsaj Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I used to twist the necklaces of the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with my hand, and then the Messenger of God would imitate them.” God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with his hand, then he will send it with my father, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, will not leave anything that God has made lawful for him until he slaughters. \the guidance\"""""
"3660","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, and Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, guides him from Medina, so he twisted the necklaces for his guidance, then he did not avoid anything of what a muhrim avoids.”"
"3661","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh and Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I used to twist the necklaces of the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then he would not avoid anything that a muhrim avoids.”"
"3662","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri reported, saying: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, told us: I heard Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, On the authority of his father, he said: Aisha said: “I used to twist the necklaces of the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would not avoid anything.” She said: Nor"
"3663","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas, who is Salam bin Sulaym, told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “ If I were to twist the chains of the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would come out with the guidance, imitating it, while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was establishing some abstains from his wives.”"
"3664","Muhammad ibn Qudamah Al-Musaysi told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said “You saw me unraveling the necklaces of sheep from the guidance of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would send them away and then he would remain lawful among us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3665","Imran ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed, he said: Shuaib ibn Ishaq informed, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed, he said: Ja`far ibn Muhammad informed me, on the authority of his father, He heard him speaking, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that he heard him speaking, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought a sacrificial animal during his Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3666","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw A man was driving a camel. He said: Ride it. He said: O Messenger of God, it is a camel. He said: Ride it. Woe to you. “On the second or third"
"3667","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Abdah bin Sulayman reported, saying: Sa`id, who is Ibn Abi Arouba, told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man driving a camel, so he said: Ride it. He said: It is a camel, he said: Ride it, he said: It is: A camel, he said on the fourth: Ride it, woe to you.”"
"3668","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Khaled told me, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man He was driving a camel, and he was too tired to walk. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a camel. He said: Ride it, even if it is a camel. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3669","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Saeed, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, “asking about riding a camel, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Ride it.” With kindness, if you resort to it until you find noon.”"
"3670","Muhammad bin Qudamah reported, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “We went out with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and we only consider Hajj. When we came to Mecca, we circumambulated the Kaaba, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered that whoever did not have a leg The sacrificial animal is permissible, so it is permissible for the one who did not bring the sacrificial animal, and whose wives did not draw water, then they are permissible. Aisha said: I had menstruated but did not circumambulate. At home, when it was the night of the measles, I said: O Messenger of God, the people return for Umrah and Hajj, and I will return for Hajj. He said: Did you not? Did you go around the nights we came to Mecca? I said: No. He said: Go with your brother to Tan’im, and perform Umrah, then your appointment will be in such-and-such place. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3671","Amr bin Ali reported to Abu Hafs, saying: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Sa’id al-Qattan, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id al-Ansari, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, thinking only that it was Hajj. When we approached Mecca, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave an order. “The one who had a sacrificial animal with him must continue his ihram, and he who did not have a sacrificial animal must remain permissible.”"
"3672","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported, saying: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “ We, the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, welcomed us by performing Hajj sincerely, as no one else was with him, by performing Hajj sincerely alone, so we arrived at Mecca on the fourth morning of the past. From Dhul-Hijjah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us and said: “Perform Ihram and perform Umrah.” So he informed him about us. We say: since it was not between us and Arafat, except for five. He ordered us to disengage and go to Mina, and our memories were dripping with semen. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and addressed us, saying: What you said has reached me, and I am most virtuous and pious of you, and had it not been for the sacrifice, I would have been permitted to make it, and if I had received from my command I would not have taken back what I had been given as a gift. He said: Ali came from Yemen and said: What did you welcome? He said: What did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, welcome? He said: So sacrifice and remain forbidden as you are. He said: Suraqa bin Jasham said: O Messenger of God, have you considered this Umrah of ours, for this year of ours or for ever? He said: It is for ever? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3673","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Ja`far, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Maysara, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Suraqa bin Malik bin Jasham, that he said: “O Messenger of God, do you think this Umrah of ours is for our years or for eternity?” The Messenger of God said. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: It is forever.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3674","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abda, meaning Ibn Sulayman, on the authority of Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, who said: Ata said: Suraqa said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had fun and we had fun with him, so we said: For us only or for eternity?” He said: “Rather, for eternity.”"
"3675","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdul Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, reported on the authority of Rabi’a bin Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Bilal, on the authority of His father, he said: “I said, ‘O Messenger of God, should I cancel the Hajj for us specifically or for people in general?’ He said: ‘Rather, for us specifically.’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3676","Amr bin Yazid Al-Basri reported, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Ayyash Al-Amiri, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, regarding Mut’ah Hajj, he said: “We had a concession.”"
"3677","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashhar reported, saying: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ja`far, reported to us, saying: Shu’bah told us, saying: I heard Abd al-Warith ibn Abu Hanifa, he said: I heard Ibrahim Al-Taymi, speaking on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, “The mut’ah of Hajj is not yours and you are not entitled to any of it.” “It was only a concession for us, the Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3678","Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari reported, saying: Ghandar reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, meaning Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: “Ta’ah was a concession for us.”"
"3679","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Baghdadi reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, saying: Mufaddal bin Muhalhalil told us, on the authority of a statement meaning Ibn Bishr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Sha’atha’, he said: I was with Ibrahim al-Nakhi and Ibrahim al-Taymi, and I said: I thought to The year unanimously agreed upon Hajj and Umrah, and Ibrahim said: If it had been your father, he would not have bothered with that. He said: And Ibrahim al-Taymi said: On the authority of his father, on the authority of my father. Dhar: “The enjoyment was only for us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3680","Abd al-A'la bin Wasil bin Abd al-A'la al-Kufi reported, saying: Abu Usama, meaning Hammad bin Usama, reported on the authority of Wahb bin Khalid, saying: He told us Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “They considered performing Umrah during the months of Hajj to be one of the most immoral debaucheries on earth. And they make the Muhrim a yellow, and they say: When the anus is healed, and the hair is freed, and the yellow comes off, or they say: Safar enters, then Umrah is permissible for whomever. He performed Umrah, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his companions came on the fourth morning of the early morning for Hajj, so he ordered them to make it an Umrah. That was with them, so they said: O Messenger of God, what is the solution? He said: The entire solution? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3681","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Ja`far Ghandar, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of a Muslim, who is al-Quray, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: “The family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to perform Umrah and the family of his companions to perform Hajj, and he ordered those who were not with him to “The sacrificial animal is permissible.” Among those who did not have the sacrificial animal was Talha bin Ubaid Allah and another man, so it was permissible. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3682","Muhammad ibn Bashar reported, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “This is an Umrah which we enjoyed. Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal should make it permissible in its entirety, as Umrah has been included in Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3683","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Nafi’, Abu Qatada’s client, on the authority of Abu Qatada: “He was with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, until he was on the road to Mecca, staying behind with his companions who were in ihram, and he was not in ihram, and he saw a wild donkey, so he sat down. On his horse, then he asked his companions to give him his whip, so he asked them for his spear, but they refused, so he took it, then he attacked the donkey and killed it, and it ate. Some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but some of them refused, so they caught up with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they asked him about that, and he said “It is only a piece of food that God has given you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3684","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs Al-Fallas, he said: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Qattan told me, he said: Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Muadh bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, he said: “We were with Talha bin Ubaid Allah while we were in ihram, so a gift was given to me.” He had a bird while he was sleeping, and some of us ate it and some of us were reluctant, so Talha woke up and saved the one who ate it, and said: We ate it with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3685","Muhammad bin Salamah reported to Abu Al-Harith Al-Masry, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading to him while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Umair Ibn Salamah Al-Dhamri said that he informed him, on the authority of Al-Bahzi, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out seeking Mecca while he was in ihram, until when They were in the spirit when a ferocious donkey appeared. This was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Leave him, for he is about to come. His companion. Al-Bahzi, who was his companion, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, may God bless you and grant him peace. What is your business with this donkey? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Abu Bakr to divide it among the companions, then he went on until it was In the middle of the night between Al-Ruwaitha and Al-Araj, when a gazelle was standing in the shade and there was an arrow in it, he claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded a man He will stand there and no one will suspect him until he passes by him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3686","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, On the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama Al-Laythi, “He presented as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a wild donkey while it was in Al-Abwa or Budan. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned it to him. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw what was on my face, he said: We did not return it. “On you except that I am forbidden.”"
"3687","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad, meaning Ibn Yazid, told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. On the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama Al-Laythi, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, approached until, when Budan, a leg of a wild donkey was brought, and he turned it away.” And he said: We are in a state of sanctity and we do not eat game. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3688","Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Rahhawi informed us, saying: Affan, meaning Ibn Muslim, informed us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, saying: Qays ibn Sa`d informed us, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Abbas said to Zayd bin Arqam: “Did you not know that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was given a hunting organ as a gift while he was in ihram, so he did not Will he accept it? He said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3689","Amr bin Ali reported to Abu Hafs, saying: I heard Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, and I heard Abu Asim Al-Nabil, meaning Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid, saying: Tell us Ibn Jurayj, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muslim told me, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Zayd bin Arqam came, and Ibn Abbas said to him: He remembers him: How did you tell me about game meat that was given as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while it was forbidden? He said: Yes, a man gave it as a gift He took a piece of meat from a game, but he took it apart and said, “We will not eat it, for we are inviolable.”"
"3690","I am Muhammad bin Qudamah Al-Masisi. He said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Al-Saab bin Jathama presented as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a donkey, a wild donkey dripping with blood, while he was in ihram, and he was with a young man. He returned it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3691","Yusuf bin Hammad Al-Ma’ni Al-Basri reported, saying: Sufyan bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, meaning Ibn Utaiba and Habib. Meaning, Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “Al-Saab bin Jathama presented a donkey to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he was in ihram, so he returned it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3692","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani narrated, saying: Khaled, meaning Ibn al-Harith, narrated to us, saying: Hisham, meaning Ibn Abi Abdullah, narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, said: “My father set out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of Hudaybiyyah So his companions entered ihram and he did not enter ihram. While I was with my companions, they laughed at each other, so I looked and saw a wild donkey, so I stabbed it. So I asked them for help, but they refused to help me, so we ate from its meat and were afraid that we would be cut off, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to raise My horse and my walk were bad, so I met a man from Banu Ghaffar in the middle of the night, and I said: Where did you leave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I left him He was talking about watering, so I caught up with him and said: O Messenger of God, your companions are reciting peace and God’s mercy upon you, and they feared that They will be herded off before you, so wait for them. So wait for them. I said: O Messenger of God, I have encountered a wild ass and I have some of it. He said to the people: Eat. And they are in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3693","Ubayd Allah ibn Fadalah informed me, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri, informed us, saying: Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salam, informed us, on the authority of Yahya ibn My father, Kathir, said: Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told me that his father told him: “He fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” The Battle of Hudaybiyyah. He said: They performed Umrah besides me, so I hunted a wild donkey and fed my companions with it while they were in Ihram, then I came. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I informed him that we have some meat that is surplus, so he said: Eat it while they are in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3694","Mahmoud bin Ghailan reported, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu`bah reported, he said: Uthman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Qatada narrated, on the authority of his father, “They were on a journey with some of them in a state of ihram, and some of them were not in a state of ihram.” He said: Then I saw a wild ass, so I mounted my horse and took a spear. I asked them for help, but they refused to help me, so I stole a whip from one of them and forced I hit the donkey and they ate from it and became compassionate. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about that and he said: Did you give advice or help? They said: No, he said: Eat it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3695","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ya’qub, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, told us, on the authority of Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of al-Muttalib, on the authority of Jabir, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Land game is lawful for you, as long as you do not hunt it or it is caught for you.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Amr ibn Abi Amr is not strong in hadith, even though Malik ibn Anas narrated from him."
"3696","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Five are not What is forbidden in killing them is a wing: the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, and the squirrel dog.”"
"3697","Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Al-Qattan, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Five people will be killed in ihram: the snake, the mouse, the kite, and the spotted crow.” “And the stubborn dog.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3698","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission to kill five people.” Of the forbidden animals: the crow, the kite, the mouse, the squirrel dog, and the scorpion.”"
"3699","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Arara told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: he told me My father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, “that a woman entered Aisha with a crutch in her hand, and she said: What is this? She said: This lizard is because the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that there was nothing that did not sting Abraham, peace be upon him, except this animal. So he commanded us to kill it, and forbade the killing of wild animals, except those with two tuffs and those with amputees, for they obliterate sight and cause loss of what is in their bellies. \Women\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3700","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id reported to Abu Qudamah al-Sarkhasi, saying: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Umar, he said: He informed me Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is no blame on the one who kills five animals for killing them while it is forbidden: “The kite, the mouse, the squirrel dog, the crow, and the scorpion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3701","Ziyad bin Ayyub Dalawayh told me, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayyub reported, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: A man said: Oh Messenger of God, what animals do we kill when we enter ihram? He said: “There are five who are not guilty of killing them: the kite, the crow, the mouse, the scorpion, and the squirrel dog.”"
"3702","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Durqi told us, he said: Hushaym, meaning Ibn Bashir Wasiti, told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked: What animals should a person in ihram kill? He said: He should kill the scorpion, the weasel, and the kite. \And the crow"," and the ungrateful dog.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3703","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: “There are five animals for which there is no blame on the one who kills them in the Sacred Mosque and in Ihram: the mouse, the kite, and the crow. And the scorpion, and the squirrel dog.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3704","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ammar, He said: “I asked Jabir bin Abdullah about the hyena and he ordered me to eat it. I said: Is it hunting? He said: Yes. I said: I heard it from the Messenger of God.” May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3705","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Dawud, who is the son of Abd al-Rahman Abu Sulaiman, told us on the authority of Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Abu Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimunah while he was in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3706","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Al-Qattan, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, he said: Amr bin Dinar told me, that Abu Al-Sha’a’a, narrated to him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had intercourse with an unlawful person.”"
"3707","Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimunah while they were in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3708","Muhammad bin Ishaq reported, saying: Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, meaning Al-Hadrami, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimuna while he was in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3709","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq al-Dimashqi and Safwan bin Amr al-Homsi told me, saying: Abu al-Mughirah told us, and his name is Abdul-Quddus. Ibn Al-Hajjaj said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimunah And he is in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3710","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Nabih bin Wahb, that Aban bin Uthman said: I heard Uthman bin Affan, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A person in ihram may not marry, propose, or marry.”"
"3711","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa’id reported, saying: Yahya ibn Sa’id al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Nafi’ informed me, on the authority of Nabih ibn Wahb, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, on the authority of his father, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade a mahram to marry, to be married, or to be engaged.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3712","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Nabih bin Wahb, who said: Omar bin Ubayd Allah bin Muammar, to Aban bin Uthman, asking him: Should a mahram be married? Aban said: Othman narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A person in ihram may not marry or be engaged.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3713","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He was cupped while in ihram.”"
"3714","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, and Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He was cupped while in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3715","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki reported on the authority of Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, who said: Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, told us: I heard Ata’. He said: I heard Ibn Abbas said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped while he was in the state of Ihram.” Then he later said: Tawoos told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he cupped The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in ihram (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3716","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Baghdadi told us, saying: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Yazid bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was cupped while in ihram because of a garment he had.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3717","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdul Razzaq reported, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He was cupped while in ihram on the back of his foot due to a bruise he had.”"
"3718","Hilal bin Bishr Al-Basri reported, saying: Muhammad bin Khalid told us, saying: Suleiman bin Bilal told us, saying: Ibn Abi Alqamah told me, that He heard Al-Araj, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Buhaynah narrating, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped the middle of his head while I was in ihram.” With the beards of a camel on the road to Mecca.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3719","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Misri and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka`b ibn Ujrah, “He was with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in ihram, and lice bothered him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to shave his head, and said: Fast. “For three days, or feed six poor people in debt, or sacrifice a sheep, whichever you do, that will suffice for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3720","Ahmad bin Saeed informed me, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah informed me, he said: Amr, who is the son of Abi Qais, informed me, on the authority of al-Zubayr, who is the son of Adi, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujrah, who said: “I entered ihram, and my head lice increased, and that reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came to me.” I was cooking something for my friends, and he touched my head with his finger and said, “Go and shave it, and give alms to six poor people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3721","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that a man was with the Prophet, who prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. Then his she-camel killed him while he was in ihram, and he died. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and shroud him. In his two garments, and do not touch him with perfume, and do not cover his head, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3722","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani narrated, saying: Khalid, meaning Ibn al-Harith, narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, and his name is Ja’far ibn Abu Wahshiyah, who is Ja`far bin Abi Iyas, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “A man in ihram was killed by his camel, and it was killed.” It was reported that he had died, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wash him with water and lotus leaves and shroud him in two garments outside his head. He said: No. “Touch him well, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah.” Shu’bah said: reciting the Talbiyah, so I asked him after ten years, and he brought the hadith as it was. He brings it, except that he said: And do not cover his face and head. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3723","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “While a man was standing at Arafat With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he fell from his camel and he crippled him, or he said: So I crippled him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: Wash him with water and lotus leaves and shroud him in two garments, and do not embalm him or cover his head, for God will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah."
"3724","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ A man in ihram clipped his she-camel and killed him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: Wash him and shroud him, and do not cover his head, nor “You must approach him in good health, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a man of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3725","Muhammad bin Muawiyah bin Malij Baghdadi reported, saying: Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifa, told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “A man was performing Hajj with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his camel’s calf died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: He will be washed and shrouded in two garments, and his head and face will not be covered, for he will rise on the Day of Resurrection, reciting the Talbiyah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3726","Imran ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed me, he said: Shuaib ibn Ishaq informed me, he said: Ibn Juraij informed me, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, That Saeed bin Jubayr told him, that Ibn Abbas told him, he said: “A forbidden man came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he proudly Then his camel was clipped and died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and put his clothes on him, and do not Cover his head, for he will come on the Day of Resurrection to respond.”"
"3727","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, the Meccan reciter, reported, saying: My father told us, he said: Juwayriyah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah bin Abdullah and Salim bin Abdullah told him that they spoke to Abdullah bin Omar, “When the army camped against Ibn al-Zubayr before he was killed, They said: It does not matter if you do not perform Hajj in public, for we fear that we will be blocked from the House. He said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but the situation was like infidels. Quraysh near the House, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered his sacrifice and shaved his head, and said: I bear witness to you that I have made it obligatory to perform Umrah. God willing, I will go. If there is space between me and the House, I will circumambulate, and if there is a barrier between me and the House, I will do what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did. I was with him, then he walked for an hour, then he said: Their affair is the same. I bear witness to you that I have made Hajj obligatory for my Umrah, but he did not permit it. from them until the Day of Sacrifice arrived and he was guided.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3728","Humayd ibn Masada reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj Al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Amr Al-Ansari said that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Whoever limps or is broken has become free, and he must have another proof.” So I asked Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurairah said about that, and they said: He is right."
"3729","Shuaib bin Yusuf Al-Nasa’i and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hajjaj Al-Sawaf, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is broken or lame is permissible and must perform Hajj from “Qabil.” I asked Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurairah, and they said: He spoke the truth, and the pronunciation is by Shuaib. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3730","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Basri reported, saying: Suwayd reported, meaning Ibn Amr, saying: Zuhayr reported, meaning Ibn Muawiyah, saying: Musa bin told us. Uqba, he said: Nafi’ told me that Abdullah bin Omar told him: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stay in Dhu Tuwa for a long time.” with it until he prays the morning prayer when he gets up to Mecca, and the place of prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is on a thick hill, and it is not of “The mosque that was built then, but below that, on a thick, rough hill.”"
"3731","Imran bin Yazid al-Dimashqi told me, on the authority of Shuaib, meaning Ibn Ishaq, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Muzahim bin Abi told me Muzahim, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muharish al-Kaabi, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out of al-Ji’ranah at night until He went out in the evening performing Umrah and became in a ji'ranah like Kaba'it, until when the sun had set, he left the ji'ranah from the belly of a saraf until he reached the road. \The city of Saraf\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3732","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muzahim, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Khalid bin Usayd, on the authority of Muhrish al-Kaabi, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out of the Jiranah at night as if it were a silver alloy, so he performed Umrah. Then he became miserable with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3733","Amr ibn Ali told Abu Hafs, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Sa`id al-Qattan, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, meaning Ibn Umar, he said: Nafi` told me, On the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Mecca from the upper gate in Batha’a and left from the lower gate.”"
"3734","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam reported, saying: Sharik told us, on the authority of Ammar al-Dahni, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He entered Mecca with a white banner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3735","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Malik told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Mecca and his sins were forgiven.” It was said: Ibn Khatal was clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba, so he said: Kill him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3736","Ubayd Allah ibn Faddalah al-Nasa’i informed me, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, meaning al-Humaydi, informed me, saying: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, informed us, saying: Malik told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Mecca in the year of the conquest, bearing the forgiven on his head.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3737","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ammar, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr Al-Makki told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca on the day of the conquest, wearing a black turban and without ihram.”"
"3738","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Bahrani narrated, saying: Hibban, meaning Ibn Hilal, narrated to us, saying: Wahib narrated to us, saying: Ayoub narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Baraa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions came to the fourth morning and were preparing for Hajj.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to dissolve.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3739","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Kathir al-Anbari, who said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Baraa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came for the past four days of Dhul-Hijjah, and he declared the fulfillment of the Hajj and performed the morning prayer with Batha’. And he said: Whoever wants to make it an Umrah, let him do so. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3740","Imran bin Yazid told me, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ata’ said: Jabir said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Mecca. On the fourth morning of Dhul-Hijjah, (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3741","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram narrated, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ja`far bin Sulaiman narrated, saying: Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he entered Mecca during the Umrah to perform the qada’, and Abdullah bin Rawaha walked in front of him, saying: Leave the children of the infidels alone. Today, we attack you for your affliction with a blow that removes inspiration from his sleep and astonishes his friend from his friend. Then Omar said to him: O son of Rawaha, in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in the Sanctuary of God, you say, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Leave it alone, for it is faster. “In them is a sprinkling of arrows.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3742","Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Musaysi told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the conquest: “This land was forbidden by God on the day He created the heavens and the earth. It is forbidden by God’s sanctity until the Day of On the Day of Resurrection, his thorns will not be bitten, his game will not be dispersed, his prey will not be picked up except by one who knows it, and his private parts will not be left alone. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, except Al-Idhkhar, and he mentioned a word that means it. He said: “Except Al-Idhkhar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3743","Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, saying: Mufaddal, meaning Ibn Muhalhalil, told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of the conquest of Mecca: “This is a forbidden country, God has made it sacred. Fighting was not permissible for anyone before me, and it was permissible for me for an hour of the day, so it is forbidden by the sanctity of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3744","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Shurayh, meaning Al-Kaabi, that he said to Amr bin Saeed And he was sending an envoy to Mecca: Allow me, O prince, to tell you something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said tomorrow from the day of My ears heard it, my heart understood it, and my eyes saw it. When he spoke of it, he thanked God and praised Him, then he said: “Indeed, Mecca God has forbidden it and people have not forbidden it. It is not permissible for a person who believes in God and the Last Day to shed blood with it or to support trees with it. Someone granted permission to fight the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so say to him: God gave permission to His Messenger but he did not give you permission, but he only gave me permission. There is an hour in the day, and its sanctity today has resumed as it was yesterday, and let the witness notify the absent person.”"
"3745","Imran bin Bakkar bin Rashid Homsi told me, he said: Bishr, meaning Ibn Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, told us, he said: My father told me, about Al-Zuhri said: Suhaim told me that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “An army will invade this house.” Then they will be swallowed up by the desert.”"
"3746","Muhammad bin Idris Al-Razi reported, saying: Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, saying: My father told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, he said: Talha bin told me Musharrif, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The missions do not stop invading the House of God until He will be overwhelmed by an army of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3747","Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Masisi told me, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Abd al-Salam told us. That is, Ibn Harb, on the authority of Al-Dalani, whose name is Yazid Abu Khaled, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of his brother, who said: Ibn Abi Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Hafsa bint Omar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A crowd will be sent to this sanctuary. So when they were in the desert of the earth, it was swallowed up first and last of them, and the middle of them was not spared. I said: What have you seen if there are believers among them? He said: It will be so They will have graves.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a strange hadith, and the one before it is strange. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3748","Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Bistami reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Umayyah bin Safwan bin Abdullah bin Safwan, he heard his grandfather say: Hafsa told me that she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let this house be secured by an army that will attack it even when they are in the desert.” From the earth, the middle of them will be swallowed up, then the first of them and the last of them will be called, and they will all be swallowed up, and only the fugitive will be saved who informs about them.” So he said to him Man: I bear witness against you that you did not lie to your grandfather, and I bear witness against your grandfather that he did not lie to Hafsa, and I bear witness against Hafsa that she You did not lie to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3749","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh reported, saying: Waki`, meaning Ibn al-Jarrah, reported, saying: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Five immoral people will be killed in the lawful and the sacred sanctuary: the crow, the kite, and the dog.” The eagle, the scorpion, and the mouse.”"
"3750","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahwayh reported, he said: An-Nadr bin Shumail reported, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab He narrates, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Five sinners will be killed in the nook and the sanctuary: the snake and the dog.” The eagle, the spotted crow, the kite, and the mouse.”"
"3751","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hafs bin Ghayath, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in fear of Mona when she came down and the messengers were known to her, so she came out alive. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Kill her. So we went to her and she went into her hole."
"3752","I am Amr bin Ali Abu Hafs, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Al-Qattan, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of his father, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of Arafat, which was before the day of Arafat, and when he felt The snake, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Kill it. It entered the crack of a burrow, so we inserted a stick and pulled out part of the burrow, so we took So we lit a fire in it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God protect you from its evil, and protect you from its evil."
"3753","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Makki reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Abdul-Hamid bin Jubayr bin Shaybah told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Umm Sharik, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to kill the lizards.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3754","Wahb bin Bayan Al-Masry reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Malik and Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The gecko is the abyssal.”"
"3755","Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid al-Raqqi told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, meaning the one-eyed son of Muhammad. Ibn Jurayj said: Aban bin Salih told me. On the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Urwa told him: that Aisha said to him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Five of the animals, all of them A sinful person shall be killed in the Sanctuary: a sterile dog, a crow, a kite, a scorpion, and a mouse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3756","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Misri reported, saying: Ibn Wahb informed me, saying: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Five animals, all of which are immoral, must be killed in the Sacred Mosque: the crow, the kite, And the squirrel dog, and the mouse, and the scorpion.”"
"3757","Issa bin Ibrahim bin Mathrud Al-Masry reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Salem bin Abd God told him: That Abdullah bin Omar said: Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no blame on the one who kills five animals: the crow, the scorpion, the kite, the mouse, and the squirrel dog.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3758","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq reported, saying: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Five sinners are to be killed in the sanctuary and in the sanctuary: the kite, the crow, the mouse, and the scorpion. And the ungrateful dog.” Abd al-Razzaq said: Some of our companions mentioned that Ma’mar used to mention him, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, Or on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3759","Ahmad bin Abdah Basri reported, saying: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zaid, told us, saying: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Five immoral people will be killed in the Sanctuary: the scorpion, the mouse, the crow, and the venerable dog. \And the kite\"""""
"3760","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Abu Ubayd Allah Makhzoumi reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is Mecca, which God made sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth. It was not lawful for anyone before me, nor For anyone after me, but it was made lawful for me for an hour of the day, and it is my hour. This is forbidden for the forbidden of God until the Day of Resurrection. Its trees are not harvested, and its hunting is not permissible except for one who seeks it. So Al-Abbas, who was an experienced man, stood up and said: Except Al-Idhkhir, for it is For our homes and our graves, and he said: Except for Al-Idhkhir."
"3761","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zangwayh reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Ja`far ibn Sulayman reported, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca during the Umrah al-Qadha, and Ibn Rawaha was in his presence, saying: Leave the children of infidels behind him today. We will strike you with a blow that removes inspiration from his bed and distracts his friend from his friend. Omar said: O Ibn Rawaha, in the sanctuary of God, and clarified The hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this poetry? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Leave it, O Omar, by the One in whose hand is my soul, according to his words. “It is more severe for them than the impact of an arrow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3762","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. The family of Banu Hashim received him. He said: He carried one in his hands and another behind him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3763","Muhammad ibn Bashar Bandar informed us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning Ghandar, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Qaza’ah al-Bahili, speaking about Al-Muhajir Al-Makki said: “Jabir bin Abdullah was asked about a man who sees a house and raises his hands? He said: I did not think anyone would do this.” Except the Jews. We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but we did not do it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3764","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, meaning Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid Al-Nabil, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abi told me Yazid, that Abd al-Rahman bin Tariq bin Alqamah told him on the authority of his mother, “Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a house Ali faced the Qiblah and supplicated.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3765","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah Al-Juhani, who said: I heard Nafi’, He said: Abdullah bin Omar told us, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere.” Of the mosques except the Sacred Mosque.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: I do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, other than Musa Al-Juhani, and Ibn Jurayj and others disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3766","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh, and Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi reported, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Ibn Juraij reported, he said: I heard Useful, he says: Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’bad told us that Ibn Abbas told him that Maimuna was the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other place except the Kaaba Mosque.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: It was narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Maimunah, and he did not mention Ibn Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3767","Amr bin Ali reported to Abu Hafs, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning treacherous, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Salama, he said: I asked Al-Aghar about this hadith, and Al-Aghar narrated that he heard Abu Hurairah narrating that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Kaaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3768","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Masry and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, that Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq informed Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Aisha The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did you not see that when your people built the Kaaba they deviated from the foundations of Abraham?” So I said: Oh Messenger of God, would you not return it to the rules of Abraham? He said: Were it not for the fact that your people had not spoken of disbelief. Abdullah bin Omar said: If it were Aisha heard this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, neglecting to receive the two pillars that The stone was softened, but the house was not completed according to the rules of Abraham. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3769","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala Al-San’ani reported on the authority of Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ubayy Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that the Mother of the Believers said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If my people had not, and in the hadith of Muhammad “Your people are new to the era of ignorance. I would have demolished the Kaaba and made two gates for it.” When Ibn al-Zubayr became king, he made two gates for it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3770","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Abdah, meaning Ibn Sulaiman al-Kufi, and Abu Muawiyah reported, saying: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “If it had not been for the recent covenant of disbelief among your people, I would have destroyed the house and built it on the foundation of Abraham, and I appointed for him a successor, for when the Quraysh built the House, they fell short.”"
"3771","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi reported, saying: Yazid bin Harun told us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim reported, saying: Yazid bin Roman told us, On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “O Aisha, had your people not been new to the covenant In ignorance, I ordered the house to be demolished, so I put into it what had been taken out of it, stuck it to the ground, and made two doors for it, an eastern door. And a western gate, for they were unable to build it, so I reached the foundation of Abraham with it.” He said: That is what prompted Ibn al-Zubayr to demolish it. Yazid said: I witnessed Ibn al-Zubayr when he demolished it, built it, and inserted stone into it. And I saw the foundation of Abraham with stones like camels’ humps interconnected. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3772","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one from Abyssinia will destroy the Kaaba.”"
"3773","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani narrated, saying: Khalid, meaning Ibn al-Harith, narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, “He reached the Kaaba, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Bilal, and Usama entered it, and Othman Ibn Usama visited them.” They opened the door, and they stayed there for a long time. Then the door was opened, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out. I rode the stairs and entered the house. I said: Where? Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray? They said: Here, and I forgot to ask them how much he prayed? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3774","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported, saying: Hushaym told us, saying: Ibn Aoun reported, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered May God bless him and grant him peace, and with him were Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, Usama ibn Zaid, Uthman ibn Talha, and Bilal. They went to the door. So he stayed among them as long as God wished, then he left. Ibn Omar said: He was the first one I met Bilal, so I said: Where did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray? He said: “What is between the two cylinders?”"
"3775","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Yahya told us, meaning Al-Qattan, saying: Al-Sa’ib bin Omar told us, saying: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, that Ibn Omar said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and he was about to leave, and I found something, so I went and came quickly, and I found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Outside, I asked Bilal: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray in the Kaaba? He said: Yes, two rak’ahs between the two pillars?"
"3776","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Abu Nu`aym, meaning Al-Fadl bin Dukain, told us, saying: Saif bin Suleiman told us, saying: I heard a mujahid saying: “The call to prayer Ibn Umar was in his house, and it was said: This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who has entered the Kaaba. He said: So I came and found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He left, and I found Bilal standing at the door, so I said: O Bilal, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray in the Kaaba? He said: Yes, I said: Where? He said: Two rak'ahs between the two pillars. Then he went out and prayed two rak'ahs in the face of the Kaaba."
"3777","Hajib ibn Sulayman al-Munbiji told me, on the authority of ibn Abi Rawwad, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Usama Ibn Zaid said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the Kaaba, swam in its outskirts, and said Allahu Akbar but did not pray, then he went out and prayed behind the shrine.” Two rak'ahs, then he said: This is the qiblah."
"3778","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: Ibn Abi Suleiman reported, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Ibn Al-Zubayr said: I heard Aisha, She says: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Had it not been that the people have entered into a covenant of disbelief, and I do not have enough money to support its construction, I would have built it.” I inserted into it five cubits of stone, and made for it a gate through which people enter, and a gate through which they exit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3779","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Rabati Maruzi told me, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Qurra bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jubayr, on the authority of his paternal aunt Safiya bint Shaybah, who said: Aisha told us, she said: “I said: O Messenger of God, should I not enter the house? He said: Enter the stone, for it is part of the House.”"
"3780","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad narrated, he said: Alqamah bin Abi Alqamah narrated to me, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “I loved to enter the house and pray there, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand and brought me into the stone, and said: Then You wanted to enter the house and pray here, for it is a part of the house, but your people were confined to where they had built it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3781","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Amr, that Ibn Abbas said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray in The Kaaba, but say takbir in its outskirts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3782","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Al-Qattan, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, he said: Ata told us, on the authority of Osama Ibn Zaid, “He and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the house, so he ordered Bilal to close the door, and the house at that time was on six floors.” Columns, then he went on until he was between the two columns next to the door of the Kaaba, and he sat down and thanked God, praised Him, asked Him, and asked for His forgiveness. Then he stood up until he reached the side of the Kaaba, and placed his face and cheek on it, and thanked God, praised Him, asked Him, and asked for His forgiveness. Then he went to every corner of the Kaaba and greeted him with the takbeer, the tahlil, the glorification, and the praise of God and the question. And asking forgiveness, then he went out and prayed two rak’ahs facing the face of the Kaaba, then he left and said: This qiblah, this qiblah.”"
"3783","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abd al-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Osama, he said: “I entered with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God grant him peace and peace in the House. He sat down and thanked God, praised Him, said “Allahu Akbar” and praised Him. Then he got up and went to the part of the House in front of him, and placed his chest on it. He touched his cheek and his hands, then he said the takbir and said hello and said supplication, and he did that with all the pillars, then he went out and faced the Qiblah while he was at the door, and he said: This kiss, this kiss.”"
"3784","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Usama, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left the House and prayed two rak’ahs facing the Kaaba, then he said: This qibla, this qibla.”"
"3785","Khushish bin Asram reported to Abu Asim, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Ibn Juraij reported, on the authority of Ata’, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: Usama bin Zaid told me, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the house and prayed in all its parts, and did not pray in it until he left it, so when He went out and performed two rak'ahs in front of the Kaaba.\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3786","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs, he said: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, he said: Al-Sa’ib bin Omar told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abd told me Allah ibn al-Sa'ib, on the authority of his father, that he used to lead Ibn Abbas and make him stand by the third apartment of the corner next to the stone next to the door, Ibn Abbas says: “Were you not informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray here? So he says: Yes, then he gets up and prays.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3787","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs, he said: Yahya al-Qattan told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, he said: Abu al-Zubair told me that He heard Jabir saying: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulating the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwah on his camel.”"
"3788","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Misri and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a reading from him, while I was hearing, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Nawfal, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: “I complained to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I am complaining, so he said: Go behind the people while you are riding. So I walked around while the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was at that time. He prays at the side of the house while reading “Al-Tur” {1} and an inscribed book {2}.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3789","Muhammad bin Adam Al-Masisi told me, on the authority of Abdah, who is the son of Sulaiman Kufi, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, he said: “ I said: O Messenger of God, by God, I have never performed the circumambulation of the exit. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: When the prayer is established, circumambulate your camel from behind. \people\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3790","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Basri narrated, saying: Suwayd bin Amr narrated, on the authority of Zuhair, who is the son of Muawiyah, who said: Bayan, who is the son of Bishr, that Wabra is Al-Kufi. He narrated to him, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, “A man asked him: Should I circumambulate the Kaaba while I have entered ihram for Hajj? He said: What prevented you? He said: I saw Abdullah bin Abbas forbidding that, and you are more surprised to us than him. He said: We saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He entered ihram for Hajj, circumambulated the Kaaba, and walked between Safa and Marwa.”"
"3791","Hanad bin Al-Sari Al-Kufi reported on the authority of Mulazim bin Amr, and he mentioned a word that means it. Abdullah bin Badr told me, he said: “I went out among people from... My companions were pilgrims until we reached Mecca, so we circumambulated the House for a week, and prayed two rak’ahs behind the shrine, when we saw a man sitting on Zamzam, and he said: Who are you? I said: From the people of the East, from the people of Al-Yamamah. He said: Did you come as pilgrims or Ammar? We said: Pilgrims. He said: So you are You invalidated your Hajj, so I said: I have performed Hajj many times and I used to do this, so I asked who is this, and they said: This is Ibn Abbas, then? We departed from there until we came to Abdullah bin Omar, and we told him what Ibn Abbas had told us, so he said: I remind you of God, as proof. Did you come or Ammar? I said: Pilgrims. He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman, all of them performed Hajj. So he did what you did.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3792","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi narrated on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Adam, who said: Sufyan, who is ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us. He said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to me. Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we did not see anything except that it was Hajj,” she said: When he circumambulated the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwah, he said: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him should perform his ihram, and whoever does not have a sacrificial animal should perform his ihram. Let him be permitted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3793","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani narrated, saying: Khaled, who is Ibn al-Harith, narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan. His name is Muslim Al-Araj. A man from Banu Al-Hujaym said to Ibn Abbas: “What is this fatwa that you give to someone who circumambulates the Kaaba? It is lawful.” He said, “The Sunnah of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, even if you wish.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3794","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi reported, saying: Bishr bin Omar Al-Zahrani told us, saying: Malik told me, and Al-Harith bin reported. Poor person. I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, and the pronunciation is his. He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Farewell Pilgrimage and we performed the Umrah. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him perform the Hajj and Umrah, then not perform it until both of them are permitted. So I came to Mecca while I was menstruating. I did not circumambulate the House, nor between Safa and Marwah. I complained about this to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Leave your hair and comb it. He invited my family to perform Hajj and leave Umrah, so I did so, and when I completed Hajj, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr. Al-Siddiq went to Tan'im, so I performed Umrah. He said: This is the place of your Umrah. So those who performed Ihram for Umrah circumambulated the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwah, then They came out, then went around another circumambulation after they had been stoned from Mina for their Hajj, and as for those who combined Hajj and Umrah, they only made one circumambulation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3795","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, who said: Hani bin Ayyub informed me, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Jabir. Bin Abdullah, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed one circumambulation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
